<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian Explorers Index climbs again in week.</title>
<headline>Australian Explorers Index climbs again in week.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1996-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Perth stockbroker Eyres Reed Ltd said its Australian Explorers Index rose 31.1 points or 0.88 percent in the week to Friday. The All Ordinaries index rose 0.95 percent.</p>
<p>Changes, in percent:</p>
<p>	    Feb  7  Jan 31   pct   1 Month  pct    1 Year  pct</p>
<p>Explorers 3570.1  3539.0 (+0.88) 3307.0 (+7.95)  2684.5(+32.99) ASX Gold  1711.7  1722.0 (-0.59) 1707.1 (+0.27)  2235.8(-23.44) All Ords  2446.7  2423.7 (+0.95) 2400.6 (+1.92)  2273.7 (+7.61) Oil &amp; Gas 1638.0  1574.6 (+4.03) 1575.3 (+3.98)  1052.1 (+55.69)</p>
<p>NOTE: The explorers index (base 500, March 1992) tracks the performance of 88 small capitalisation exploration companies.</p>
